from_correspondance is control data shared by Mahendrawada in 082026
in response to a query about control data used in the GEO accession.

This does recreate the peaks/results nearly exactly using this 
workflow AND including the mito reads.
The following settings were used to create the components in
`from_correspondance`:

- dmel coverage: sbatch --array=3 mahendrawada_checseq_pipeline/01b_dmel_normalized_coverage.sh mahendrawada_checseq_pipeline/freemnase_lookup.txt full

Which uses full alignment (including chrM)

- tag_dir: sbatch mahendrawada_checseq_pipeline/maketagdir_control.sh results/bams/from_correspondance/A/from_correspondance_A.bam results/bams/from_correspondance/A/from_correspondance_A_samtools_stats.txt --authors_orig

Which also uses the full alignment and despite passing in the samtools stats, it allows homer to infer fragment length and 
genome size to match original author's scripts

- 5p filtering and coverage: in this case, this is only the nuclear locations b/c the 'include regions' used (and provided)
  only includes the nuclear chr. Note that this is used for promoter enrichment, not recreating the authors results

- align: both the yeast alignment, and then the unmapped reads are aligned to the dmel using the scripts provided here directly. 
